[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629611275","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102337#issuecomment-2629611275","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102337","id":2629611275,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cvK8L","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-02T23:25:53Z","updated_at":"2025-02-02T23:25:53Z","body":"See the \"Transparency Sorting\" section of the [3d rendering limitations page](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.html#transparency-sorting) in the docs. \n\nLabel3D is transparent by default whether you use a solid color or not. It needs to be transparent otherwise it would just draw a big rectangle. \n\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629611275/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629719464","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102337#issuecomment-2629719464","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102337","id":2629719464,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cvlWo","user":{"login":"Sithoid","id":131390156,"node_id":"U_kgDOB9TazA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131390156?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sithoid","html_url":"https://github.com/Sithoid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sithoid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sithoid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sithoid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sithoid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sithoid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sithoid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sithoid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sithoid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sithoid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-03T01:51:31Z","updated_at":"2025-02-03T01:51:31Z","body":"I guess this leaves two questions:\n1) Since the outline is a default feature, what's the intended use? Manual sorting by depth whenever the objects move, like in my last example?\n2) Would it help to have separate settings for the label and the outline, or perhaps a different way to implement the outline other than a second plane on the next layer? Seems like with the current implementation there's basically no way to keep the text and the outline together, since if you assign them the same render priority, they start clashing with each other.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629719464/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray"